================================================================================

==============	
 DATA QUALITY
==============

LINEAGE:
COMPASS Instrument Properties represent properties with inforce Licences and/or Permits issued under the Rights in Water and Irrigation Act 1914. The underlaying layer is determined by the property type and is sourced from Cadastre property boundary provided by Landgate; Current (Live and Pending) Mining Tenements comprising surveyed and unsurveyed tenements managed by Department of Mines industry Regulation and Safety; and spatially linked database of agricultural and other properties maintained by the Department of Primary Industries and Regional Development (DPIRD). Property boundaries may also be based on property types not listed above managed by respective property custodians. 

The Cadastre dataset is maintained and updated from accurate survey information lodged in digital form and stored in the Spatial Cadastral Database(SCDB). It combines polygons of the same land+AF8-id and pi+AF8-parcel (land parcel identifier) into single multi-polygon "land" features. ie:pi-parcel += one "land" += one record in the data. LAND refers to an area of land that the State has an interest in administering. As well as lots created on freehold or crown survey plans, it also covers other land of interest such as reserves, leases, road isolations, unallocated crown land and stock routes. Land areas may comprise more than one polygon and may be over lapping - e.g. a parcel of land that is a crown lot covered by a timber reserve as well as State Forest.


Updates:
Compass was commissioned in June 2018 and is subject to regularly enhancements and bug fixes.

POSITIONAL ACCURACY:
Accurate representation of License and/or Permit properties issued under the Rights in Water and Irrigation Act 1914. COMPASS Instrument Properties are consistent with property boundaries of land types listed above as of date of Licence/Permit issue. Changes made to underlaying land boundaries may occur during licence duration. Digitised data is accurate to 1mm at source map scale (Landgate).

ATTRIBUTE ACCURACY:
COMPASS Instrument Properties are validated by the custodian and represent the accurate location of properties associated with Licence and/or Permits issued under the Rights in Water and Irrigation Act 1914 at the time of issue.

LOGICAL CONSISTENCY:
Polygon dataset, based on Cadastral property boundaries.

COMPLETENESS:
Complete.


